.TH I420 2
.SH NAME
i420 \- convert YCbCr 4:2:0 video frames to RGB
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "i420.m";
i420 := load I420 I420->PATH;

rgb24: fn(y, cb, cr: array of byte, w, h: int, out: array of byte);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B I420
is built into the emulator.
It converts video frames in planar YCbCr 4:2:0 (I420) form,
as video decoders deliver them
(see
.BR /appl/cmd/vid9p.b ),
to pixels for a
.B Draw->RGB24
image.
.PP
.B Rgb24
converts a frame
.I w
by
.I h
pixels, both even, from its planes:
.I y
holds
.IB w * h
luma samples, row by row;
.I cb
and
.I cr
each hold
.IB w /2* h /2
chroma samples, one for each 2 by 2 block of pixels.
It stores
.IB 3* w * h
bytes in
.IR out ,
three for each pixel in the order blue, green, red,
which is how
.B RGB24
lays out a pixel in memory, ready for
.BR Image.writepixels .
The coefficients are those of JPEG (full range BT.601),
in 16-bit fixed point.
.PP
.B Remap24
in
.B /appl/mpeg
uses
.B I420
when it can be loaded and converts in Limbo when it cannot,
with the same arithmetic: the pixels are the same either way,
only faster here.
.SH SOURCE
.B /libinterp/i420.c
.br
.B /appl/mpeg/remap24.b
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B Rgb24
raises an exception if a plane is nil,
if
.I w
or
.I h
is not positive and even,
or if a plane or
.I out
is too small for the frame.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR draw-image (2)
